    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25963" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lătĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		later, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to bricks, brick-</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra lateraria,</span>”
				<i>brick-clay</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 8, 45, § 156</span></i>
			.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lătĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
				ĭi, m., <i>a
				brickmaker</i>, <i><span class="en">Non. 445,
			22</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lătĕ-rārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f. (sc. officina), <i>a brickkiln</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56, 57, §
		194</span></i>.</div>
